the control: a toned label paints NOTHING in the untoned fg,
so the ink below is the tone being obeyed and not a coincidence.
  none  in default fg = 140
  error in default fg = 0

a toned label paints in its tone's colour, not the style fg:
  none ink=140 color=13421772
  error ink=140 color=13369344
  success ink=140 color=3394560
  warning ink=140 color=13408512

the tone survives the layout pass and the other decorators:
  set-tone then set-flex: 4
  set-flex then set-tone: 4
  default on a fresh node: 0
